I've grepped the code for instances of charisma checks, and I've found
that having a high charisma only:

1) Reduces the amount of gold required to bribe soldiers
2) Allows you to resist succubus seduction.
3) Decreases shop prices.
4) Increase chance of mounting a steed.

And that's it!

Personally, judging from this, I don't think charisma is worth
measuring or checking in the game for what little influence it has. I
think point number 2 is illogical (resisting seduction should be
entirely a test of will - i.e wisdom) and point 3 (shop prices) has
always been influenced more by obnoxious shirts and your level of
hunger. Sure, replacing the charisma markup with a straight x2, give or
take class or alignment-specific markups, would make price-ID easier,
but it's not as if the existing system goes out of its way to make
price-ID hard.



